From: koalabuttz <27229333+koalabuttz@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 05:26:43 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix: refuse a negative index in the script parser's error
 recovery

yyerrlab1 looks up the error token at yycheck[yypact[state] + 1]. Eight
states have a yypact value below -1 (down to -50), and the lower bound
test was dropped, so recovery in one of them read up to 49 entries in
front of yycheck. Put the "< 0" test back beside the upper bound.

Recovery only runs when CompileError returns, which is the script
debugger's expression evaluation; a normal compile leaves through
Com_Error first.
---
 src/script/scr_yacc2.cpp | 3 +--
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/script/scr_yacc2.cpp b/src/script/scr_yacc2.cpp
index ae07d668..0f49dc2e 100644
--- a/src/script/scr_yacc2.cpp
+++ b/src/script/scr_yacc2.cpp
@@ -2049,8 +2049,7 @@ yyerrlab1:
 			goto yyerrpop;
 		}
 
-		//if (++yyn < 0 || yyn > 0x543 || yycheck[yyn] != 1) // 0x59B on t5
-		if (++yyn >= 0x544 || yycheck[yyn] != 1) // LWSS CHANGE
+		if (++yyn < 0 || yyn >= 0x544 || yycheck[yyn] != 1) // 0x59B on t5
 		{
 			goto yyerrpop;
 		}
